  "source_level_notes": [
    "The design-time TopPipe and BottomPipe instances visible in Continuous and Chaves layout XML are destroyed by event SID 2246972820014324 at layout start. The first runtime pair is spawned by event SID 6640649658259165 after SECONDSPEROBSTACLE seconds.",
    "The source project has exactly three layouts. Chaves is last in project order, so Go to next layout is a no-op at Required_Score.",
    "The source project declares Facebook and Browser plugins but the checked-in Event Sheets contain no actions or conditions for those plugins.",
    "Google Play SignIn is used on Android in Start events. This port exposes a callback boundary and an offline fallback; it does not claim to include a configured Google Play Games SDK client.",
    "Original media bytes are intentionally pending. Audio/font integrations resolve project-relative paths and emit warnings while placeholders are empty.",
    "The generic Construct 2/3 importer is explicitly out of scope for this round. This event coverage is a hand-authored mapping of the one known Flappy Madruga project.",
    "The retry parent event and its Queda-guarded child are root events after the six named groups; they are not a seventh Construct event group.",
    "The Chaves layout-start animation event must be considered together with the included Common in-game layout-start Destroy actions. Construct 2 treats Destroy as deferred until event-sheet processing completes; the editor-time pipe instances therefore do not establish a skin for later timer-created instances. The Rust gameplay model keeps spawned pipe pairs on Default animation until a differential run proves otherwise.",
    "Construct 2 defaults to max dt=1/30 second for per-tick and behavior movement. Every-X-seconds and Wait are time-based System events and must not be accumulated from the capped movement dt."
  ]
}
